{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts","id":963801,"title":"Possible Host Concepts?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-05T11:11:52-07:00","id":963801,"title":"Possible Host Concepts?","content":"Hey all Korogra here, how are you? As you know there are various Shartha on these forums such as Chris' Ukusgualu, Claire's Zibhesi, Cinder's Bharsalu and Suthilu as well as my Gisilu ( I think someone made an interesting, if mechanicless Moth Host too... but can't remember the name), but I was wondering, what sort of Host concepts have been thought up by you guys?<br /> <br /> I have an inkling of two new potential shartha concepts in my head that would be pretty cool, though not sure how to bring them to life. <br /> <br /> One is a very Uratha-centric Flea Host that is able to transmit Kuruth to humans and animals alike while aggravating the Death Rage of werewolves.<br /> <br /> The other is a centipede-host that can somehow infest ghosts, using them as puppets while causing the Gauntlet to rot, leading the Hisil and Underworld to bleed into each other, which then affects the living world.<br /> <br /> Any ideas on how to make these spirit-hosts work would be incredibly helpful, as well as hearing about whatever cool, horrifying shartha critters any of you have thought up!! That would be greatly appreciated. <br /> <br /> As always thanks and don't forget to share your thoughts! Have a wonderful day!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T12:05:36-07:00","id":963830,"title":"","content":"Orchid Host from the Amazonian rainforest. They scatter their seeds in the Shadow, and hitch a ride on shapeshifters or other hosts crossing the Gauntlet, or sometimes on humans that pass through verges. From there, they materialize as spiny seeds in the real world, and dig into human bodies like hookworms do if they come in contact with human skin. When the seeds burst through with vines and flower, they drive their victims to seek out verges and other places where the Gauntlet is thin, so that they can collect ulal from the spirit world like water condensation in the air. They're not antagonist automatically, and actually have a symbiotic relationship with Beshilu \u2014 some Rat Hosts tend to &quot;gardens&quot; of them where they've worn down the Gauntlet. Others feed and follow them around to find holes in the Gauntlet they can wear down around and pass through easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T12:38:16-07:00","id":963847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=963830#post963830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Orchid Host from the Amazonian rainforest. They scatter their seeds in the Shadow, and hitch a ride on shapeshifters or other hosts crossing the Gauntlet, or sometimes on humans that pass through verges. From there, they materialize as spiny seeds in the real world, and dig into human bodies like hookworms do if they come in contact with human skin. When the seeds burst through with vines and flower, they drive their victims to seek out verges and other places where the Gauntlet is thin, so that they can collect ulal from the spirit world like water condensation in the air. They're not antagonist automatically, and actually have a symbiotic relationship with Beshilu \u2014 some Rat Hosts tend to &amp;quot;gardens&amp;quot; of them where they've worn down the Gauntlet. Others feed and follow them around to find holes in the Gauntlet they can wear down around and pass through easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like that idea, its like the Fungus Hosts while being not nearly as tortuous..and being much prettier! How do you think they interact with Uratha? I also wonder what sort of pretty/creepy things the hybrids do when not feeding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T17:38:00-07:00","id":963987,"title":"","content":"Cicada hosts who sleep inside their hosts for months and months until they eventually drive them to reach the tallest place they can and burst out of them leaving a calcified hust. These monstrous insectiods then start to beat their drums, creating a sound that resonates through the gauntlet resulting in other shartha being ripped into the area and the area's shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T18:37:36-07:00","id":964005,"title":"","content":"Cat Hosts<br /> <br /> There are many legends of a werewolf's bite turning a person into a werewolf. Though the Uratha know this only makes some people into Wolf Blooded when they're infected with Lunacy, these Sharatha take that story a bit more literally. Those attacked by and bitten by a werecat become infected with a feline spirit of vengence, which slowly takes over the body over the course of a fortnight, transforming into a full therianthrope. <br /> <br /> Though called the Cat Hosts, the truth is that all hosts have three forms - the house cat form, human form, and a large predator cat form, be it a lion, a tiger, a jaguar, a panther, or other large cat. Each Host is &quot;born&quot; when a new human is infected, and the host must be a consumed with a desire for vengence. Only someone that's been wronged so deeply and utterly that they snapped can become a cat Host; only those driven by a desire for revenge can sucessfully nurish such essence until their very mind and body are consumed into a new being. <br /> <br /> Often, a cat host will immediately seek to fulfill their &quot;parent's&quot; wish for vengence. Which is all well and good, but then comes the problem - the Host is still driven by a spirit's need for food and a human biological need to have children, forcing it to hunt down others with a desire for vengence to create more of their kind, and to engage in a perverse spirit hunt on those targets of revenge for essence. Unfortunately, the feline hosts have no inbuilt sense of balance - if left unchecked, the hosts seek out and kill for the slightest infractions, irregardless of why, and create huge communities of felines that spread out in their search for food.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T19:45:34-07:00","id":964026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=963847#post963847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really like that idea, its like the Fungus Hosts while being not nearly as tortuous..and being much prettier! How do you think they interact with Uratha? I also wonder what sort of pretty/creepy things the hybrids do when not feeding.</div> </div> </div> </div>When they're not feeding, they exist in a state of torpor. The flowers close up, and they stand around limply like living meat puppets. (Think the remotely-controlled bodies from Playdead's <i>Inside, </i>or the brain worm-controlled bodies from<i> Limbo.</i>) They will react to being attacked with a poisonous pollen spray and thorny, whipping vines, but they're not actively malicious or threatening. For your average Forsaken, such as a Hunter In Darkness, it would be a pretty easy case of chopping up the weeds if the host seeds didn't drop and spread everywhere like kudzu. If you're Pure, on the other hand, you might be tempted to keep a few of these things around as living essence collectors for yourself, your totem and your troops. You can harvest the ulal very, very carefully if you're gentle about it.<br /> <br /> Don't try eating the flowers, though \u2014 their makeup in the<i> Gurihal </i>is a lot like human flesh, so that would be a breaking point. There's also the fact of the brain and nervous system being the first thing taken over by the Host, but it can be hit-or-miss whether the human feels anything. Some go into a coma, some become brain-dead very quickly, and some are trapped in a dreaming state, like the effects of the Black Mercy Flower from the <i>Justice League</i> series. Sometimes, the human feels and is aware of everything, to a wide variety of degrees, but is helpless to do anything.<br /> <br /> I'm not entirely sure on the full effects of the flowers/pollen when harvested. The ulal has a tinge of plant essence to it, so you could feed it directly to to totems and spirits that subsist on that kind of essence. You'd have to purify it a little before you gave it to anything else, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 09-05-2016, 10:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T21:47:55-07:00","id":964067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=963987#post963987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cicada hosts who sleep inside their hosts for months and months until they eventually drive them to reach the tallest place they can and burst out of them leaving a calcified hust. These monstrous insectiods then start to beat their drums, creating a sound that resonates through the gauntlet resulting in other shartha being ripped into the area and the area's shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, so they act as a rallying cry for other Hosts, or do they just rile the others up to ridiculous degrees?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T21:51:04-07:00","id":964069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=964005#post964005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cat Hosts<br /> <br /> There are many legends of a werewolf's bite turning a person into a werewolf. Though the Uratha know this only makes some people into Wolf Blooded when they're infected with Lunacy, these Sharatha take that story a bit more literally. Those attacked by and bitten by a werecat become infected with a feline spirit of vengence, which slowly takes over the body over the course of a fortnight, transforming into a full therianthrope. <br /> <br /> Though called the Cat Hosts, the truth is that all hosts have three forms - the house cat form, human form, and a large predator cat form, be it a lion, a tiger, a jaguar, a panther, or other large cat. Each Host is &amp;quot;born&amp;quot; when a new human is infected, and the host must be a consumed with a desire for vengence. Only someone that's been wronged so deeply and utterly that they snapped can become a cat Host; only those driven by a desire for revenge can sucessfully nurish such essence until their very mind and body are consumed into a new being. <br /> <br /> Often, a cat host will immediately seek to fulfill their &amp;quot;parent's&amp;quot; wish for vengence. Which is all well and good, but then comes the problem - the Host is still driven by a spirit's need for food and a human biological need to have children, forcing it to hunt down others with a desire for vengence to create more of their kind, and to engage in a perverse spirit hunt on those targets of revenge for essence. Unfortunately, the feline hosts have no inbuilt sense of balance - if left unchecked, the hosts seek out and kill for the slightest infractions, irregardless of why, and create huge communities of felines that spread out in their search for food.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh hey, the Colony! Very interesting interpretation of a 1st ed splat. How do werewolves view them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T21:57:23-07:00","id":964073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=964067#post964067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting, so they act as a rallying cry for other Hosts, or do they just rile the others up to ridiculous degrees?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rallying cry, since cicada's do the drone as a mating call and it probably wants more cicada shartha to merge with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T22:05:18-07:00","id":964075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=964026#post964026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When they're not feeding, they exist in a state of torpor. The flowers close up, and they stand around limply like living meat puppets. (Think the remotely-controlled bodies from Playdead's <i>Inside, </i>or the brain worm-controlled bodies from<i> Limbo.</i>) They will react to being attacked with a poisonous pollen spray and thorny, whipping vines, but they're not actively malicious or threatening. For your average Forsaken, such as a Hunter In Darkness, it would be a pretty easy case of chopping up the weeds if the host seeds didn't drop and spread everywhere like kudzu. If you're Pure, on the other hand, you might be tempted to keep a few of these things around as living essence collectors for yourself, your totem and your troops. You can harvest the ulal very, very carefully if you're gentle about it.<br /> <br /> Don't try eating the flowers, though \u2014 their makeup in the<i> Gurihal </i>is a lot like human flesh, so that would be a breaking point. There's also the fact of the brain and nervous system being the first thing taken over by the Host, but it can be hit-or-miss whether the human feels anything. Some go into a coma, some become brain-dead very quickly, and some are trapped in a dreaming state, like the effects of the Black Mercy Flower from the <i>Justice League</i> series. Sometimes, the human feels and is aware of everything, to a wide variety of degrees, but is helpless to do anything.<br /> <br /> I'm not entirely sure on the full effects of the flowers/pollen when harvested. The ulal has a tinge of plant essence to it, so you could feed it directly to to totems and spirits that subsist on that kind of essence. You'd have to purify it a little before you gave it to anything else, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>My mind spins with the possibilites this idea has. Especially that thing with the Pure. Sacrilege in its absolute finest. Wolves don't permit shartha to persist, so doing that is surely going to call a butt ton of Hunters in Darkness AND their Blood Talon meatshields/friends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T22:15:04-07:00","id":964078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=964073#post964073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rallying cry, since cicada's do the drone as a mating call and it probably wants more cicada shartha to merge with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it only draw other cicadas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T22:22:29-07:00","id":964081,"title":"","content":"Seems like they might be a nice harvest for Claimed, especially giant Hive-Claimed. The idea of malformed giants 'plucking' shartha-infested people from storehouses and downing them for fuel is grossly appropriate.<br /> <br /> I've liked a lot of the homebrewed hosts but I've always had trouble thinking out specifics for them myself. So far I've only really come up with a few ideas that were never fleshed out. The Fire Hosts, based on the story Afterburn by Tim Curran. They represent a fairly immediate threat, as opposed to the creeping plague of most hosts. Like wildfire, they spread, infecting as many others as they can with the fire that burns but doesn't die. It gets worse and worse over a short period of time, the hosts don't last more than twelve hours, until they infest enough to spawn a great conflagration that sears the Gauntlet forever and die out in the process.<br /> <br /> There was another idea for a host that wasn't on Earth before or during the Sundering and later found themselves stuck in a void. They left but haven't been able to return. They really exist as their own 'kind' more than the other shartha. They lack personalities beyond mindless Essence-eaters until one has absorbed enough of their own kind and becomes capable of taking over bodies, including other supernaturals, and determining what they want for themselves or others. They were based on the Daemonites, from Wildstorm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-06-2016, 01:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T22:29:01-07:00","id":964084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=964078#post964078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does it only draw other cicadas?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, whatever types of shartha are nearby. Just might be some cicadas amoung the nearby gauntlet, might not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T22:44:08-07:00","id":964086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=964081#post964081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems like they might be a nice harvest for Claimed, especially giant Hive-Claimed. The idea of malformed giants 'plucking' shartha-infested people from storehouses and downing them for fuel is grossly appropriate.<br /> <br /> I've liked a lot of the homebrewed hosts but I've always had trouble thinking out specifics for them myself. So far I've only really come up with a few ideas that were never fleshed out. The Fire Hosts, based on the story Afterburn by Tim Curran. They represent a fairly immediate threat, as opposed to the creeping plague of most hosts. Like wildfire, they spread, infecting as many others as they can with the fire that burns but doesn't die. It gets worse and worse over a short period of time, the hosts don't last more than twelve hours, until they infest enough to spawn a great conflagration that sears the Gauntlet forever and die out in the process.<br /> <br /> There was another idea for a host that wasn't on Earth before or during the Sundering and later found themselves stuck in a void. They left but haven't been able to return. They really exist as their own 'kind' more than the other shartha. They lack personalities beyond mindless Essence-eaters until one has absorbed enough of their own kind and becomes capable of taking over bodies, including other supernaturals, and determining what they want for themselves or others. They were based on the Daemonites, from Wildstorm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like both of those ideas, I think the &quot;elemental&quot; shartha idea has a lot of potential in particular.<br /> <br /> The second idea is pretty intriguing due to how alien it sounds. We have rats, spiders, crabs, locusts and what not, but they at least resemble things in nature. Not these monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T22:48:50-07:00","id":964088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=964084#post964084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, whatever types of shartha are nearby. Just might be some cicadas amoung the nearby gauntlet, might not.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty cool concept, makes clearing them out problematic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T02:07:46-07:00","id":964157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=964069#post964069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh hey, the Colony! Very interesting interpretation of a 1st ed splat. How do werewolves view them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm personally fond of turning all the different animal-types from Skinchangers and WatP into Hosts. So, yep! Here's the Colony.<br /> <br /> Well, primarily there's three things that came to mind as I wrote this. First is some debate as to if these cats actually are Hosts, or should be considered a form of Claimed, so there's some argument between Tribes about who has &quot;jurisdiction&quot; as prey. There's a bit of blurring of lines. <br /> <br /> Secondly? While the werewolves as a whole aren't opposed to the idea of cat hosts in theory, its clear that they create an imbalance with their vengence seeking, as revenge begets more revenge in a vicious, destructive cycle, which clearly goes against the Uratha duty of maintaining balance. That imbalance is the primary reason that the cat hosts are classified as hosts instead of something akin to the Uratha themselves. <br /> <br /> Third, given anger issues, its not unheard of that the Uratha themselves become targets of the cat hosts. Interestingly, the Pure themselves end up being targetted more than the Forsaken, given the former's more brutal and domineering tendacies towards others. As a result, there's actually factions of the Blood Talons that are interested in cultivating the cat hosts as weapons or fellow warriors against their enemies instead of just prey to balance out. Insert rumors of turning cat hosts into cat shifters through rites and moon spirit intercessions, depending on player inclinations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T03:21:56-07:00","id":964183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=964157#post964157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm personally fond of turning all the different animal-types from Skinchangers and WatP into Hosts. So, yep! Here's the Colony.<br /> <br /> Well, primarily there's three things that came to mind as I wrote this. First is some debate as to if these cats actually are Hosts, or should be considered a form of Claimed, so there's some argument between Tribes about who has &amp;quot;jurisdiction&amp;quot; as prey. There's a bit of blurring of lines. <br /> <br /> Secondly? While the werewolves as a whole aren't opposed to the idea of cat hosts in theory, its clear that they create an imbalance with their vengence seeking, as revenge begets more revenge in a vicious, destructive cycle, which clearly goes against the Uratha duty of maintaining balance. That imbalance is the primary reason that the cat hosts are classified as hosts instead of something akin to the Uratha themselves. <br /> <br /> Third, given anger issues, its not unheard of that the Uratha themselves become targets of the cat hosts. Interestingly, the Pure themselves end up being targetted more than the Forsaken, given the former's more brutal and domineering tendacies towards others. As a result, there's actually factions of the Blood Talons that are interested in cultivating the cat hosts as weapons or fellow warriors against their enemies instead of just prey to balance out. Insert rumors of turning cat hosts into cat shifters through rites and moon spirit intercessions, depending on player inclinations.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is pretty interesting. The only thing that I find that clashes with what could be considered Host is how its a shsoeshifter. Besides that, its very interesting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T04:19:05-07:00","id":964210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=964183#post964183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is pretty interesting. The only thing that I find that clashes with what could be considered Host is how its a shsoeshifter. Besides that, its very interesting</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, when 1e first came out, I pegged the Sharatha as alternative-spider and rat shifters. I've used the rules for Hosts as a base for all kinds of non-Wolf shifters for a long time now, long before WatP came out. Its inevitable that its going to inform my view of how the Hosts act and their abilities. Naturally, I understand that its non-cannon, but its how I've done it for a long time now. Spiders, rats, cats, ravens, snakes, turtles, bears... I've run all of them as hosts at some point or another. I even have some Pangaean progenitor legend somewhere in my notes for each.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 09-06-2016, 07:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T04:32:09-07:00","id":964214,"title":"","content":"My own idea for a scorpion host was based on a documentary about the Egyptian King Scorpion - it included a snippet about why he might have taken the name, ie what qualities of a scorpion's reputation was he trying to lay claim to - and the suggestion made was its endurance and toughness. So in the &quot;one verb&quot; model of a host - where the rats gnaw, the crows watch, and the locusts consume - the scorpions endure.<br /> <br /> That means defend themselves of course, and they will. They don't generally seek out their own kind to grow in power, though they will interpret any other they come across as a threat. Werewolves too, usually, but it's not impossible to make deals with them. They are predators of course, and hunt humans. But what a lot of them want is to shape the environment around them into walls of armour and security - this makes them more likely than other hosts to get involved with the human world and try to shape it to their advantage (thus King Scorpion could have been a scorpion host).<br /> <br /> Like the Halaku, scorpion hosts at the lower end of power control a possessed human from afar rather than burrowing into them. Naturally, rather than eating the eyes, this is accomplished via stinging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T08:48:18-07:00","id":964317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=964210#post964210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, when 1e first came out, I pegged the Sharatha as alternative-spider and rat shifters. I've used the rules for Hosts as a base for all kinds of non-Wolf shifters for a long time now, long before WatP came out. Its inevitable that its going to inform my view of how the Hosts act and their abilities. Naturally, I understand that its non-cannon, but its how I've done it for a long time now. Spiders, rats, cats, ravens, snakes, turtles, bears... I've run all of them as hosts at some point or another. I even have some Pangaean progenitor legend somewhere in my notes for each.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair I suppose, its a pretty interesting way to handle Hosts. In fact, the Unclean practically embody that idea. At the same time, a cat literally burrowing into a person and hijacking their body is way more scary/funny XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T08:51:28-07:00","id":964320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=964214#post964214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My own idea for a scorpion host was based on a documentary about the Egyptian King Scorpion - it included a snippet about why he might have taken the name, ie what qualities of a scorpion's reputation was he trying to lay claim to - and the suggestion made was its endurance and toughness. So in the &amp;quot;one verb&amp;quot; model of a host - where the rats gnaw, the crows watch, and the locusts consume - the scorpions endure.<br /> <br /> That means defend themselves of course, and they will. They don't generally seek out their own kind to grow in power, though they will interpret any other they come across as a threat. Werewolves too, usually, but it's not impossible to make deals with them. They are predators of course, and hunt humans. But what a lot of them want is to shape the environment around them into walls of armour and security - this makes them more likely than other hosts to get involved with the human world and try to shape it to their advantage (thus King Scorpion could have been a scorpion host).<br /> <br /> Like the Halaku, scorpion hosts at the lower end of power control a possessed human from afar rather than burrowing into them. Naturally, rather than eating the eyes, this is accomplished via stinging.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that idea, I always thought that there should be a Scorpion Host. Now, do they alter the Gauntlet in any way to help &quot;fortify&quot; their lairs- or does that sound too Azlu?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T13:10:25-07:00","id":964487,"title":"","content":"Huh, I thought of another!<br /> <br /> Machine Hosts- Remnants of a primordial spirit/pangean who represented humanity's latent innovative greatness, the Machine Hosts in their base form resemble sapient, highly animate tiny bits of technology ( biomechanical microchips, screws etc). These intelligent pieces of junk infest humans like all shartha do by burrowing into a mortal, where they begin converting the brain and other organs into bizarre mechanisms that are equal parts flesh and metal as they assert control over the body.<br /> <br /> Strange and considered to be unhinged even by Host standards, the machine-shartha are driven by three imperatives: to intergrate more and more complex pieces of machinery into their fleshy forms, to &quot;upgrade&quot; other organic creatures ( usually fatal) and to build nonsensical, dangerous occult devices.<br /> <br /> Because of these driving instincts, the Machine Hosts oddly refrain from consuming each other unless driven to by an outside threat, and thus are quite communal much like the Beshilu. This compounds the dangers posed by the machine shards greatly, for while a single host may cause havok as it tinkers about... when several gather together the result of their &quot;work&quot; can be catastrophic for an area.<br /> <br /> Why the hosts do these things is not well understood. Aside from assimilating new technology into themselves, their other goals seem to serve no clear purpose. The people and animals the Machine Hosts &quot;improve&quot; normally simply die and the machines they build are usually non-functional; but the exceptions that exist are often nightmarish and deadly. If Spiders weave and Rats gnaw, it could be said that Machines &quot;build&quot; or &quot;innovate&quot; - as bloody or pointless their creations may be.<br /> <br /> ( I sort of envision these guys to be sort of like the Borg or Strogg from Quake, a good antagonist for both Hunters in Darkness and Iron Masters)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 09-06-2016, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T17:00:37-07:00","id":968831,"title":"","content":"aww, it's sort of sad that no one had any suggestions for the centipedes or fleas <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T17:27:16-07:00","id":968847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=968831#post968831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">aww, it's sort of sad that no one had any suggestions for the centipedes or fleas <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>One of the reasons I've had trouble with hosts, a lack of what to do with them. Azlu weave up the Gauntlet, beshilu gnaw it away. The lampreys turn it to blood, sort of. Is doing 'something' to the Gauntlet something all hosts do? In first edition it didn't seem so. The fungal hosts just lived, the worm hosts ate away morality.<br /> <br /> I found it hard to find a unifying thread beyond 'small things that parasitize humans, but maybe they just eat other small things and grow big instead.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T17:40:55-07:00","id":968856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=968847#post968847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the reasons I've had trouble with hosts, a lack of what to do with them. Azlu weave up the Gauntlet, beshilu gnaw it away. The lampreys turn it to blood, sort of. Is doing 'something' to the Gauntlet something all hosts do? In first edition it didn't seem so. The fungal hosts just lived, the worm hosts ate away morality.<br /> <br /> I found it hard to find a unifying thread beyond 'small things that parasitize humans, but maybe they just eat other small things and grow big instead.'</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't have to, though many seem to be connected to it in strange ways. What is a big thing with Hosts that I find unifying is that they are all broken, distorted reflects of the Uratha; Half flesh hybrids that attempt to emulate their progenitor. The biggest difference is that the Hosts are, like stated.. broken.<br /> <br /> That spirit/ flesh and man/animal hybrid nature being twisted to nightmarish proportions by the Host's life cycle is just really cool too lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T21:50:59-07:00","id":969007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=968856#post968856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They don't have to, though many seem to be connected to it in strange ways. What is a big thing with Hosts that I find unifying is that they are all broken, distorted reflects of the Uratha; Half flesh hybrids that attempt to emulate their progenitor. The biggest difference is that the Hosts are, like stated.. broken.<br /> <br /> That spirit/ flesh and man/animal hybrid nature being twisted to nightmarish proportions by the Host's life cycle is just really cool too lol</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am working on a type of Azlu that attaches itself to humans, and it lays its eggs inside of them until they hatch. Trying to decide if it necessarily kills the person, or if they burst out of them. This way you can have these horrifically injured, souless former &quot;hosts&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Running: <a href=\"https://shield-bearers.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Shield Bearers - W:TF 2nd</a><br /> Currently Planning: The Dead End Kids - CoD<br /> Untilted Tenra Bansho Zero game<br /> Currently Playing: <a href=\"http://theunusualsuspects.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Unusual Suspects - D:td</a>, I am playing <a href=\"http://www.noordinaryobsession.com/2016/08/19/unusual-suspects-naturalist/\" target=\"_blank\">The Naturalist</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2293-salientmind","name":"salientmind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T05:33:56-07:00","id":969159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>salientmind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=969007#post969007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am working on a type of Azlu that attaches itself to humans, and it lays its eggs inside of them until they hatch. Trying to decide if it necessarily kills the person, or if they burst out of them. This way you can have these horrifically injured, souless former &quot;hosts&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you ever feel like making them something other than spiders, wasps would fit the bill here. (Just about the only thing that could make Fortitude even more of a nightmare fuel than it already is).<br /> <br /> <br /> While &quot;kudzu host&quot; sounds goofy to me, on an aesthetic level, a Host based on an aggressive plant, that just grows and grows and grows - a Host that's potentially apocalyptic for your territory. Or maybe one based on strangler vines that throttles the life out of a region. The symptoms might look a but like the Azlu thickening the Gauntlet, but in truth, threads of this Host are threading along the currents of essence, appropriating them and making loci run dry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T08:52:15-07:00","id":969245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>salientmind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=969007#post969007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I am working on a type of Azlu that attaches itself to humans, and it lays its eggs inside of them until they hatch. Trying to decide if it necessarily kills the person, or if they burst out of them. This way you can have these horrifically injured, souless former &quot;hosts&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that idea, though perhaps, though instead of Azlu, what if it were some sort of tape worm or round worm-host?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T08:54:33-07:00","id":969247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=969159#post969159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you ever feel like making them something other than spiders, wasps would fit the bill here. (Just about the only thing that could make Fortitude even more of a nightmare fuel than it already is).<br /> <br /> <br /> While &quot;kudzu host&quot; sounds goofy to me, on an aesthetic level, a Host based on an aggressive plant, that just grows and grows and grows - a Host that's potentially apocalyptic for your territory. Or maybe one based on strangler vines that throttles the life out of a region. The symptoms might look a but like the Azlu thickening the Gauntlet, but in truth, threads of this Host are threading along the currents of essence, appropriating them and making loci run dry.</div> </div> </div> </div>... or wasps, that's even better!<br /> <br /> I like the idea of more flora based Hosts, Sikla's Orchid Host idea being a favorite of mine, and I like the idea of Kudzu creepers growing from locus to locus to locus, draining them dry while causing the Gauntlet to calcify is pretty cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T11:41:02-07:00","id":969343,"title":"","content":"I have an idea about an Idigam that catches Hosts and transform them into things other than Spiders and Rats, which also changes what how they fundamentally work. Basically a plot device to keep all the Host lore being focused on just Bishilu and Azlu, but new Hosts cropping up because once created the new Host types have a life cycle that allows them to multiply.<br /> <br /> The rules of thumb that I've made for Hosts is that they all can take control of humans via an organ that represents control, Brain, Heart, Stomach, Eyes, ect... That those organs shouldn't overlap with other Host types, and the organ should be tied to the symbolism of the Host's drive.<br /> <br /> I've made a matching pair of Host types, Cockroach Hosts, and Squirrel Hosts that control their hosts in a particularly grotesque ways, They are biologically sex specific due to the symbolism. Cockroaches Breed as their primary drive(which is manifest in rapid spreading of the smallest type of this Host), and Squirrels Collect (which is manifest as the ability to collect multiple organs from many individuals and influence/control them all). For obvious reasons these particular horrors are not Parental Guidance Rated game friendly, but worked as a way to extrapolate the design principles.<br /> <br /> I really like the Aggressive Plant idea, and think the Spine would be the organ I'd assign them, with a Drive to Connect (with each other to create networks/briar patches). The Loci drying up just being a side effect of the massive resources it takes to fuel them.<br /> <br /> (Squirrel Host by the way will be featured in <i>Shadows Over Longview,</i> a fan setting book about my home town.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://viktorb.files.wordpress.com/2008/09/img_2415.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://viktorb.files.wordpress.com/2008/09/img_2415.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://viktorb.files.wordpress.com/2008/09/img_2415.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://viktorb.files.wordpress.com/2008/09/img_2415.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://viktorb.files.wordpress.com/2008/09/img_2425.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://viktorb.files.wordpress.com/2008/09/img_2425.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://viktorb.files.wordpress.com/2008/09/img_2425.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://viktorb.files.wordpress.com/2008/09/img_2425.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://lvsquirrelfest.com/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://lvsquirrelfest.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/cropped-Untitled-design-1.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://lvsquirrelfest.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> Squirrel Fest &ndash; Celebrating Squirrels, Family, and Friends and Everything Nutty </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://lvsquirrelfest.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://lvsquirrelfest.com/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-14-2016, 04:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T11:41:26-07:00","id":969344,"title":"","content":"I do plan on finishing my Moth Host one day, and I did thought about making a Scorpion Host, although focusing on them as healers and judges of purity- those who survive their poison are pure, and come back stronger. Those who don't...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T11:44:24-07:00","id":969346,"title":"","content":"I've wondered, is it possible to have an host based on something else than a living creature???<br /> For exemple, an ... i don't know, electricity host???","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T11:48:59-07:00","id":969348,"title":"","content":"They are supposedly based on Pangaeans, and we do have conceptual Pangaeans, so yes. There's also rumored to be ghost hosts. And one of the possible hosts is the host of the 'Clutter.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T03:44:04-07:00","id":969799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=969343#post969343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rules of thumb that I've made for Hosts is that they all can take control of humans via an organ that represents control, Brain, Heart, Stomach, Eyes, ect... That those organs shouldn't overlap with other Host types, and the organ should be tied to the symbolism of the Host's drive.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a very good principle.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T07:25:52-07:00","id":969883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=969343#post969343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rules of thumb that I've made for Hosts is that they all can take control of humans via an organ that represents control, Brain, Heart, Stomach, Eyes, ect... That those organs shouldn't overlap with other Host types, and the organ should be tied to the symbolism of the Host's drive.</div> </div> </div> </div>... And <i>that</i> concept just helped me expand a bit more on an idea I've been working on for a few weeks.<br /> <br /> (Mind, I came into Werewolf with the release of 2e, and with only very limited knowledge of established Hosts from 1e or info about them, I don't know if the following is redundant or something.)<br /> <br /> As mentioned a few posts above, the Hosts are more than likely the fragments of not-quite-slain Pangaeans, and with the latter's absence in the modern day it's very unlikely any new Host &quot;species&quot; could possibly come into being... but that doesn't mean we can't have something fascinated enough with them that it tries to join their number regardless, no?<br /> <br /> Enter an Idigam I've been poking at for a little while now, whose experiments are all dedicated to the end-goal of becoming a Host (Ant in particular; I'm sure someone else thought of it long before me, official material or otherwise, but hopefully my own take on it holds up okay), intentionally instead of out of desperation like the Azlu and Beshilu presumably did. The Idigam itself has some history and preliminary stats outlined, but now I've started expanding on the hypothetical end result beyond spitballed bullet-points.<br /> <br /> I figure the Ant Host's &quot;thing&quot; would be to scour the Flesh and the Shadow alike for essence (represented in part by the &quot;Devourer&quot; Dread Power being their &quot;signature&quot;, corresponding to &quot;Gauntlet Web&quot; or &quot;Gnaw Gauntlet&quot; for the Azlu and Beshilu respectively). They'd also build large nests around loci that they'd proceed to taint with the essence they harvested, and link those poisoned loci together to expand their feeding range (and as such, an established colony always has a bloated &quot;queen&quot; Shard with Locus Manipulation, and older hybrids semi-frequently develop it as well, despite Essence-Shaping appearing to be beyond the usual reach of non-Idigam). What I wasn't too sure about was the precise details of their hybrids, but thanks to the quoted concept I've nailed it down to them nesting in the abdominal cavity of the unfortunate mortal fleshbag, starting in the stomach, and compelling them to eat anything they can remotely fit down their throat. Of course, every single scrap gets converted into essence for the Ants by way of their, ah, broad palette, so the mortal slowly starves while they themselves multiply and colonize the entire gut, organ by organ, before migrating through the rest of the body. Mature hybrids are, of course, something to behold - heavy mandibles protruding around broken, yellowed teeth; too many eyes glittering in each socket; extra limbs with too many joints; skin covered in chitinous plates, or bristly hairs, or thousands of tiny, twitchy, useless wings; countless ants pouring into and out of every orifice... real charmers, you get the idea.<br /> <br /> Side note: Individual shards aren't very bright and colonies tend to be focused on sating their collective appetites, but hybrids tend to develop a curious streak and taste for tinkering echoing their kind's former nature, often hungering for esoterica and freakish experimentation almost as intensely as they do for flesh and ephemera. Unlike other hosts, they don't really want to restore their original form in its entirety, as that would defeat the purpose of being Hosts to begin with, but they do maintain contact with others of their kind so as to expand their collective knowledge and to constantly remind themselves just how hard-pressed a hypothetical force would be to wipe them out as they are now.<br /> <br /> (Long story short, I wanted to mix two of my favorite antagonist types - the Idigam and the Hosts - and this is part of the outcome of that. I'm not terribly familiar with the game though, so I can't help but shake the feeling I've missed several things.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:03:15-07:00","id":970194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=969344#post969344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do plan on finishing my Moth Host one day, and I did thought about making a Scorpion Host, although focusing on them as healers and judges of purity- those who survive their poison are pure, and come back stronger. Those who don't...</div> </div> </div> </div>I look forward to the moths, they are interesting.<br /> <br /> Death, mutation, all that jazz?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:04:15-07:00","id":970195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=969348#post969348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are supposedly based on Pangaeans, and we do have conceptual Pangaeans, so yes. There's also rumored to be ghost hosts. And one of the possible hosts is the host of the 'Clutter.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Or of apathy or any wonderfully terrible thing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:07:22-07:00","id":970197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sconce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=969883#post969883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... And <i>that</i> concept just helped me expand a bit more on an idea I've been working on for a few weeks.<br /> <br /> (Mind, I came into Werewolf with the release of 2e, and with only very limited knowledge of established Hosts from 1e or info about them, I don't know if the following is redundant or something.)<br /> <br /> As mentioned a few posts above, the Hosts are more than likely the fragments of not-quite-slain Pangaeans, and with the latter's absence in the modern day it's very unlikely any new Host &amp;quot;species&amp;quot; could possibly come into being... but that doesn't mean we can't have something fascinated enough with them that it tries to join their number regardless, no?<br /> <br /> Enter an Idigam I've been poking at for a little while now, whose experiments are all dedicated to the end-goal of becoming a Host (Ant in particular; I'm sure someone else thought of it long before me, official material or otherwise, but hopefully my own take on it holds up okay), intentionally instead of out of desperation like the Azlu and Beshilu presumably did. The Idigam itself has some history and preliminary stats outlined, but now I've started expanding on the hypothetical end result beyond spitballed bullet-points.<br /> <br /> I figure the Ant Host's &amp;quot;thing&amp;quot; would be to scour the Flesh and the Shadow alike for essence (represented in part by the &amp;quot;Devourer&amp;quot; Dread Power being their &amp;quot;signature&amp;quot;, corresponding to &amp;quot;Gauntlet Web&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;Gnaw Gauntlet&amp;quot; for the Azlu and Beshilu respectively). They'd also build large nests around loci that they'd proceed to taint with the essence they harvested, and link those poisoned loci together to expand their feeding range (and as such, an established colony always has a bloated &amp;quot;queen&amp;quot; Shard with Locus Manipulation, and older hybrids semi-frequently develop it as well, despite Essence-Shaping appearing to be beyond the usual reach of non-Idigam). What I wasn't too sure about was the precise details of their hybrids, but thanks to the quoted concept I've nailed it down to them nesting in the abdominal cavity of the unfortunate mortal fleshbag, starting in the stomach, and compelling them to eat anything they can remotely fit down their throat. Of course, every single scrap gets converted into essence for the Ants by way of their, ah, broad palette, so the mortal slowly starves while they themselves multiply and colonize the entire gut, organ by organ, before migrating through the rest of the body. Mature hybrids are, of course, something to behold - heavy mandibles protruding around broken, yellowed teeth; too many eyes glittering in each socket; extra limbs with too many joints; skin covered in chitinous plates, or bristly hairs, or thousands of tiny, twitchy, useless wings; countless ants pouring into and out of every orifice... real charmers, you get the idea.<br /> <br /> Side note: Individual shards aren't very bright and colonies tend to be focused on sating their collective appetites, but hybrids tend to develop a curious streak and taste for tinkering echoing their kind's former nature, often hungering for esoterica and freakish experimentation almost as intensely as they do for flesh and ephemera. Unlike other hosts, they don't really want to restore their original form in its entirety, as that would defeat the purpose of being Hosts to begin with, but they do maintain contact with others of their kind so as to expand their collective knowledge and to constantly remind themselves just how hard-pressed a hypothetical force would be to wipe them out as they are now.<br /> <br /> (Long story short, I wanted to mix two of my favorite antagonist types - the Idigam and the Hosts - and this is part of the outcome of that. I'm not terribly familiar with the game though, so I can't help but shake the feeling I've missed several things.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually did a write up Ant Hosts awhile back ( The Gisilu), if you would like to see how I did them. This concept you've is pretty interesting, and not terribly different from my own... I'd love to read this if you ever did I write up!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:14:34-07:00","id":970207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=969343#post969343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have an idea about an Idigam that catches Hosts and transform them into things other than Spiders and Rats, which also changes what how they fundamentally work. Basically a plot device to keep all the Host lore being focused on just Bishilu and Azlu, but new Hosts cropping up because once created the new Host types have a life cycle that allows them to multiply.<br /> <br /> The rules of thumb that I've made for Hosts is that they all can take control of humans via an organ that represents control, Brain, Heart, Stomach, Eyes, ect... That those organs shouldn't overlap with other Host types, and the organ should be tied to the symbolism of the Host's drive.<br /> <br /> I've made a matching pair of Host types, Cockroach Hosts, and Squirrel Hosts that control their hosts in a particularly grotesque ways, They are biologically sex specific due to the symbolism. Cockroaches Breed as their primary drive(which is manifest in rapid spreading of the smallest type of this Host), and Squirrels Collect (which is manifest as the ability to collect multiple organs from many individuals and influence/control them all). For obvious reasons these particular horrors are not Parental Guidance Rated game friendly, but worked as a way to extrapolate the design principles.<br /> <br /> I really like the Aggressive Plant idea, and think the Spine would be the organ I'd assign them, with a Drive to Connect (with each other to create networks/briar patches). The Loci drying up just being a side effect of the massive resources it takes to fuel them.<br /> <br /> (Squirrel Host by the way will be featured in <i>Shadows Over Longview,</i> a fan setting book about my home town.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://viktorb.files.wordpress.com/2008/09/img_2415.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://viktorb.files.wordpress.com/2008/09/img_2415.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://viktorb.files.wordpress.com/2008/09/img_2415.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://viktorb.files.wordpress.com/2008/09/img_2415.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://viktorb.files.wordpress.com/2008/09/img_2425.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://viktorb.files.wordpress.com/2008/09/img_2425.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://viktorb.files.wordpress.com/2008/09/img_2425.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://viktorb.files.wordpress.com/2008/09/img_2425.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://lvsquirrelfest.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://lvsquirrelfest.com/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I have a lot of reading to do, it seems","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T15:07:15-07:00","id":970260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=970194#post970194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I look forward to the moths, they are interesting.<br /> <br /> Death, mutation, all that jazz?</div> </div> </div> </div>among others- but their major theme is sleep, nightmares and hallucinations. The original, crunch-less draft is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444981-viskthaigilu-the-moth-host\">here</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T15:28:40-07:00","id":970275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=970197#post970197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually did a write up Ant Hosts awhile back ( The Gisilu), if you would like to see how I did them. This concept you've is pretty interesting, and not terribly different from my own... I'd love to read this if you ever did I write up!</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, and here I half-hoped I was being a little clever.. that's pretty humbling. ^^;<br /> Awh well... suppose my weird little variant kinda begs to have more Idigam-ness mixed in anyhow so it's not basically just &quot;oh by the by they were an Idigam whose plans worked and yeah&quot;. I'll have to see if I can do a write-up sometime for their predecessor form and some of its connections and experiments for the Idigam thread, and maybe slip details in for the hypothetical Host state somewhere toward the end.<br /> If that doesn't feel like enough... there's probably some room to shift it over to, say, a Wasp Host instead, though that'd call for heavier revisions in general. And I'm sure that exists somewhere too, since parasitic wasps are creepy as it is and it'd be easy enough to ramp that horror up by making them sentient God-motes.<br /> <br /> I do wonder just how far one could push the Hosts = Parasites thing... Virus Hosts could be a weird and freaky option. Spreading supernatural disease among those touched by the Shadow in any way, maybe? With some mind-tampering, as well...? Or could leave that last one to Earwig Hosts I suppose, as a spin-off of old urban legends. Or I suppose you could consider weeds to be akin to parasites in certain contexts, which opens up the very bizarre option of Willow Hosts... or my favorite for the combination of absurdity, potentially complex and weird life cycle, and opportunity to make something cheery yellow scary, Dandelion Hosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":". 09-15-2016, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T10:09:57-07:00","id":970762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sconce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=970275#post970275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahh, and here I half-hoped I was being a little clever.. that's pretty humbling. ^^;<br /> Awh well... suppose my weird little variant kinda begs to have more Idigam-ness mixed in anyhow so it's not basically just &quot;oh by the by they were an Idigam whose plans worked and yeah&quot;. I'll have to see if I can do a write-up sometime for their predecessor form and some of its connections and experiments for the Idigam thread, and maybe slip details in for the hypothetical Host state somewhere toward the end.<br /> If that doesn't feel like enough... there's probably some room to shift it over to, say, a Wasp Host instead, though that'd call for heavier revisions in general. And I'm sure that exists somewhere too, since parasitic wasps are creepy as it is and it'd be easy enough to ramp that horror up by making them sentient God-motes.<br /> <br /> I do wonder just how far one could push the Hosts = Parasites thing... Virus Hosts could be a weird and freaky option. Spreading supernatural disease among those touched by the Shadow in any way, maybe? With some mind-tampering, as well...? Or could leave that last one to Earwig Hosts I suppose, as a spin-off of old urban legends. Or I suppose you could consider weeds to be akin to parasites in certain contexts, which opens up the very bizarre option of Willow Hosts... or my favorite for the combination of absurdity, potentially complex and weird life cycle, and opportunity to make something cheery yellow scary, Dandelion Hosts.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/884923-gisilu-the-ant-host\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...u-the-ant-host</a><br /> <br /> Well, when I made these things there were a couple of people who were wanting to do an Ant-Host, but when I just happened to do it first, they all decided that there was no need for them to do it- an Ant-Host was already in place for the homebrew lol. Still, your idea is unique enough to be noteworthy up here on the forums. Now I do say again that there definitely needs to be a parasitic wasp Host.. that idea is just far too appropriate to go ignored this long,<br /> <br /> Eh.. while I'm not too keen on the idea of a virus-host, disease spirits fill that niche more effectively, the idea of an Earwig Host or a Dandelion Host is pretty intriguing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T14:23:21-07:00","id":970916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=970260#post970260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">among others- but their major theme is sleep, nightmares and hallucinations. The original, crunch-less draft is in <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444981-viskthaigilu-the-moth-host&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></div> </div> </div> </div>And binge eating","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T14:30:02-07:00","id":970918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=970916#post970916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And binge eating</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For binge eating i'd see a caterpillar host who burrows in someone's stomach and just eat non-stop to transform into ... something else (just had the idea and i didnt think that far yet )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T14:31:15-07:00","id":970919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=970918#post970918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> For binge eating i'd see a caterpillar host who burrows in someone's stomach and just eat non-stop to transform into ... something else (just had the idea and i didnt think that far yet )</div> </div> </div> </div>I think LostLight would agree with you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T17:30:45-07:00","id":971011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=970762#post970762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/884923-gisilu-the-ant-host\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...u-the-ant-host</a><br /> <br /> Well, when I made these things there were a couple of people who were wanting to do an Ant-Host, but when I just happened to do it first, they all decided that there was no need for them to do it- an Ant-Host was already in place for the homebrew lol. Still, your idea is unique enough to be noteworthy up here on the forums. Now I do say again that there definitely needs to be a parasitic wasp Host.. that idea is just far too appropriate to go ignored this long,<br /> <br /> Eh.. while I'm not too keen on the idea of a virus-host, disease spirits fill that niche more effectively, the idea of an Earwig Host or a Dandelion Host is pretty intriguing</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oof... that's a <i>very</i> impressive bit of homebrew there. O.o<br /> <br /> Huh... It's... kind of odd that nobody seems to have actually done a Wasp Host yet. Almost a crime against homebrew. Not entirely sure what they'd do if I were to structure them myself, but of course they'd be very nasty and very, <i>very</i> visceral doing it, even for a Host.<br /> <br /> - - - - - - -<br /> <br /> Dandelion Hosts were admittedly kind of a half-joke at first, but thinking about it they could prove a genuine issue despite not having the mobility of animal-themed <i>shartha</i>... crowding out natural plants by attracting pollinators to them instead, contaminating the air with &quot;pollen&quot; that in turn warps local resonance and possibly threatens to taint spirits in the local Twilight, infecting allergy-prone or otherwise at-risk mortals and producing hybrids at a distance through that same pollen... there's a <i>lot</i> they could get up to. And yet, given the flower has history as a medicinal herb, they could probably be harvested at a certain point in their life cycle for various purposes. Which of course means that ambitious werewolves (or mages, in crossover), probably at the suggestion and encouragement of a Dandelion hybrid itself, have probably tried to find ways to safely cultivate them.<br /> <br /> <i>Tried.</i><br /> <br /> There's also potential for weird, visceral horror in the design of Dandelion Host hybrids, in part because of just how disparate animal and plant anatomy are. Flowers growing out of eye sockets; root systems spread throughout the body and twisting out of the scalp in a mockery of hair; clouds of noxious pollen trailing behind them as they move and breathe; sticky, milky sap instead of blood, working both to clot wounds quickly and impair an attacker; the skin coated in patches of petals or white parachute-seeds that occasionally let go and drift off, potentially to become a new shard and start the cycle elsewhere...<br /> <br /> Their history might take some clever work to make, well... work, but they could easily be the fragments of a Pangaean linked to Fertility or Spring that went a bit overboard. Overall I'm mostly spitballing at the moment and taking some notes, but... there's definitely material to work with and plenty of room to work in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":".  Somehow managed to delete two entire sentences somewhere in the writing process. Oops. 09-16-2016, 08:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T21:27:58-07:00","id":971139,"title":"","content":"These things exist, I've seen 'em. It's not exactly the most popular thing to say, mind you: there are hunters out there that maybe do what we do but do it better than us. If anything's a candidate, though, it's them. The <i>Abazu</i>, the Mantis Hosts. Their legends are kind of scary. They say that no Wolf-Father came for their progenitor. These things were just too badass. The world changed, so did they. Most everything got smaller, but here's the thing: it didn't get any less hungry.<br /> <br /> Abazu are nasty buggers, and I mean that literally. You almost don't notice they're there. They can blend in so well on either side of the Gauntlet, and if the stories are to be believed, they even sometimes hunt <i>inside </i>the Gauntlet. Yeah, imagine that. Things in there that shouldn't be, and these things that <i>really </i>shouldn't be are in there eatin' 'em. Or other things that try to cross over. Spirits, Claimed, witches, werewolves, what-the-fuck-ever goes where it shouldn't, suddenly you might find yourself locked in the arms of one of these guys.<br /> <br /> They don't hate. Not us, at least. They don't particularly seem to dislike us, any more than they do anyone or anythin' else. Makes it all the creepier when they're eatin' your friend, or that prey you've been chasin' for a couple days. Just complete ice. No fear, no rage, no emotion as they tie something up and begin to eat it. Faster than anything you've ever seen, too. No, I don't care what. No vampires, no lightning-spirit, nothin'. Absolutely nothing comes close to how fast the Abazu can grab you. They move so fast the Gauntlet sometimes opens up in their wake, like they sliced it right open. Just usually means more food for them. And once you're locked in, ain't nothin' is gettin' you back out unless you have your pack nearby.<br /> <br /> What do they want? To eat. Man, they just eat the supernatural, and don't care what it is. If it's magic, it's mealtime. What I wonder is just what they're doin' with all that energy, you know? Are they building up these stores of power to do something with some day? If so, what? The old sayin' goes that you are what you eat, yeah? These things eat anything mystical that wanders into their clutches. What's that make them, huh? What do they want? Knowledge? More power? I'll tell ya what I <i>do </i>know it makes 'em.<br /> <br /> Hungry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T06:35:03-07:00","id":971298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=971139#post971139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These things exist, I've seen 'em. It's not exactly the most popular thing to say, mind you: there are hunters out there that maybe do what we do but do it better than us. If anything's a candidate, though, it's them. The <i>Abazu</i>, the Mantis Hosts. Their legends are kind of scary. They say that no Wolf-Father came for their progenitor. These things were just too badass. The world changed, so did they. Most everything got smaller, but here's the thing: it didn't get any less hungry.<br /> <br /> Abazu are nasty buggers, and I mean that literally. You almost don't notice they're there. They can blend in so well on either side of the Gauntlet, and if the stories are to be believed, they even sometimes hunt <i>inside </i>the Gauntlet. Yeah, imagine that. Things in there that shouldn't be, and these things that <i>really </i>shouldn't be are in there eatin' 'em. Or other things that try to cross over. Spirits, Claimed, witches, werewolves, what-the-fuck-ever goes where it shouldn't, suddenly you might find yourself locked in the arms of one of these guys.<br /> <br /> They don't hate. Not us, at least. They don't particularly seem to dislike us, any more than they do anyone or anythin' else. Makes it all the creepier when they're eatin' your friend, or that prey you've been chasin' for a couple days. Just complete ice. No fear, no rage, no emotion as they tie something up and begin to eat it. Faster than anything you've ever seen, too. No, I don't care what. No vampires, no lightning-spirit, nothin'. Absolutely nothing comes close to how fast the Abazu can grab you. They move so fast the Gauntlet sometimes opens up in their wake, like they sliced it right open. Just usually means more food for them. And once you're locked in, ain't nothin' is gettin' you back out unless you have your pack nearby.<br /> <br /> What do they want? To eat. Man, they just eat the supernatural, and don't care what it is. If it's magic, it's mealtime. What I wonder is just what they're doin' with all that energy, you know? Are they building up these stores of power to do something with some day? If so, what? The old sayin' goes that you are what you eat, yeah? These things eat anything mystical that wanders into their clutches. What's that make them, huh? What do they want? Knowledge? More power? I'll tell ya what I <i>do </i>know it makes 'em.<br /> <br /> Hungry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you me from an alternate universe where I masquerade as Chris Redfield's sister as I write freelance stuff.. and somehow got sucked into this reality? Because I've been trying to do a Mantis Host for awhile.<br /> <br /> (Somewhat xD ) Joking aside, you totally should do a full write up of this, this concept is too cool","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T06:37:26-07:00","id":971301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sconce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=971011#post971011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oof... that's a <i>very</i> impressive bit of homebrew there. O.o<br /> <br /> Huh... It's... kind of odd that nobody seems to have actually done a Wasp Host yet. Almost a crime against homebrew. Not entirely sure what they'd do if I were to structure them myself, but of course they'd be very nasty and very, <i>very</i> visceral doing it, even for a Host.<br /> <br /> - - - - - - -<br /> <br /> Dandelion Hosts were admittedly kind of a half-joke at first, but thinking about it they could prove a genuine issue despite not having the mobility of animal-themed <i>shartha</i>... crowding out natural plants by attracting pollinators to them instead, contaminating the air with &quot;pollen&quot; that in turn warps local resonance and possibly threatens to taint spirits in the local Twilight, infecting allergy-prone or otherwise at-risk mortals and producing hybrids at a distance through that same pollen... there's a <i>lot</i> they could get up to. And yet, given the flower has history as a medicinal herb, they could probably be harvested at a certain point in their life cycle for various purposes. Which of course means that ambitious werewolves (or mages, in crossover), probably at the suggestion and encouragement of a Dandelion hybrid itself, have probably tried to find ways to safely cultivate them.<br /> <br /> <i>Tried.</i><br /> <br /> There's also potential for weird, visceral horror in the design of Dandelion Host hybrids, in part because of just how disparate animal and plant anatomy are. Flowers growing out of eye sockets; root systems spread throughout the body and twisting out of the scalp in a mockery of hair; clouds of noxious pollen trailing behind them as they move and breathe; sticky, milky sap instead of blood, working both to clot wounds quickly and impair an attacker; the skin coated in patches of petals or white parachute-seeds that occasionally let go and drift off, potentially to become a new shard and start the cycle elsewhere...<br /> <br /> Their history might take some clever work to make, well... work, but they could easily be the fragments of a Pangaean linked to Fertility or Spring that went a bit overboard. Overall I'm mostly spitballing at the moment and taking some notes, but... there's definitely material to work with and plenty of room to work in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Run, the puffballls are rising up against us!<br /> <br /> This idea is pretty good, I like it.<br /> <br /> And I appreciate that you find it impressive, though it did take a lot of time to actually bring it all together.. life is not a fair mistress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T16:40:02-07:00","id":971570,"title":"","content":"Wasp Host idea: Strange, parastic creatures that can't create their own vessels, so they have to hunt down and infect other Hosts to actually do anything. The Hunters are divided in how to respond to this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T17:55:46-07:00","id":971613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=971570#post971570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasp Host idea: Strange, parastic creatures that can't create their own vessels, so they have to hunt down and infect other Hosts to actually do anything. The Hunters are divided in how to respond to this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dig it. Wasps are cool and creepy; Wasp Hosts would be evil, evil bastards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T07:40:26-07:00","id":971924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=971570#post971570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasp Host idea: Strange, parastic creatures that can't create their own vessels, so they have to hunt down and infect other Hosts to actually do anything. The Hunters are divided in how to respond to this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do they get to make use other shartha dread powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T11:04:22-07:00","id":972021,"title":"","content":"One of my earliest nightmares as a child was, after seeing too much National Geographic, about a huge parasitic wasp who lay its eggs in humans- in sort, I approve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T01:48:01-07:00","id":972405,"title":"","content":"I wonder what Great Mountain's shartha would be like....<br /> My first thought is dust that takes hold of humans that breathe them in. The dust causes them to constantly be coughing up soil, their veins turn to iron, and a stone spire starts to grow from their heart until it burst out of their back. Eventually a large group of this soil filled hosts should get together and mindlessly start construction of massive stone structures that mystically increase the spread of the mountain shards further across the land.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T05:45:06-07:00","id":972462,"title":"","content":"When thinking about Mountain's shartha, I can't but think about the cannibal children from Elysium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T09:26:51-07:00","id":972570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=972462#post972462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When thinking about Mountain's shartha, I can't but think about the cannibal children from Elysium.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did too, though it was less obvious to me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T09:34:34-07:00","id":972575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=972405#post972405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder what Great Mountain's shartha would be like....<br /> My first thought is dust that takes hold of humans that breathe them in. The dust causes them to constantly be coughing up soil, their veins turn to iron, and a stone spire starts to grow from their heart until it burst out of their back. Eventually a large group of this soil filled hosts should get together and mindlessly start construction of massive stone structures that mystically increase the spread of the mountain shards further across the land.</div> </div> </div> </div>These things are totally Tiberium! Im imagining these giant stony spires/artificial Mountains to covered in veins of crystalized Essence, the tops of Which that billow vast clouds of these Infant Hosts.. which would be pretty cool. I also imagine that they could have an obsession with digging too, discovering rich hidden places of the Spirit and Flesh.. perfect material to add to their spires.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T12:13:22-07:00","id":974584,"title":"","content":"Termite Hosts<br /> <br /> Few among the People know of the horribly dangerous Ant Hosts, but those Elders of the Hunters in Darkness who do sometimes tell a little known legend of the Gisilu's Warrior Progenitor. While the Pangean known as the Warrior was an entity of death an ruination, it also held dominion over new life and rebirth, which makes the fact that the ant-hosts only seem to focus on destruction highly peculiar - though loremasters have a simple answer: The death of the Warrior did not mark the birth of one breed of shartha.. but two.<br /> <br /> The termite hosts are rare, but like their ant cousins they congregate in large numbers, though their purpose couldn't be any more different. Where the ants kill and raze and decimate the spiritual and material worlds around them, the termites instead work to sustain the spiritual world and to help it thrive. While they will devour humans and kill that which threatens them as all Hosts do, the termite-shartha are much more concerned with their instinctual imperative to nourish the Shadow. While on the surface this does not seem to be so bad, and in fact sounds to be quite beneficial.. the truth, as always, is not so simple. How the shartha accomplish this feat is both elegant and disruptive, the hosts locate a locus and set up shop on its Hisil side, from there they build towering nests that greatly resemble chimneys, which serve to funnel spiritual energies and Resonance from the material world and convert it into Essence which billows from the tops of these 'chimneys' as great multicolored clouds that settle down on the surrounding spiritscape. This process is not without drawbacks, and the material world suffers for it; people and animals in the vicinity of these nests grow increasingly listless and lethargic, and objects and structures in the surrounding area are subjected to accelerated structural deterioration. Even worse, the termites use humans as living batteries and amplifiers for their chimney-nests, and their Hybrids are known to be some of the most variable and adaptable of any breed of shartha, including their Gisilu cousins, each successive generation growing more and more adept at protecting their nests from outside aggressors with ever-evolving bio-spiritual weaponry.<br /> <br /> Despite the threat to a local area should these monsters set down roots, they possess a dilemma for many Uratha. While the Meninna will undoubtedly move to destroy these abominations, as will Iron Masters for the threat to their territories, other packs might, <b>might</b>, be tempted to let these things persist for a little while, reassured that the vast influx of new Essence will alow the material side to eventually recover once the termites have finished serving a packs designs. This practice is far more commonly implemented by the Pure than the Forsaken, as many Anshega view the termites to be beneficial, so long as they are strictly controlled and contained... a prospect that often proves to be more difficult than they anticipate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 09-22-2016, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T14:10:38-07:00","id":974653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=971570#post971570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasp Host idea: Strange, parastic creatures that can't create their own vessels, so they have to hunt down and infect other Hosts to actually do anything. The Hunters are divided in how to respond to this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Brilliant! I was trying to think of a way to keep the parasite-egg-layer theme in a category where even creatures that aren't innate parasites become parasitic by physiological possession. Parasite of Parasite does that nicely. I'd also strongly tie this to the Wasps Host's procreation.<br /> <br /> I could totally see an Ant Version which is the same with Vegetation based Host, all Leaf-Cutter style, but they cultivate the Vegetation Host's so they don't run out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T16:44:49-07:00","id":975274,"title":"","content":"Extravagant beehives, dripping with honey, but anything that tastes some slowly has bees manifest from inside their organs, effectively turning the victim into a sort of Bee Host as a step towards making them into a new hive. The victim actually forms the center of the hive, with the traditional hive structure built around them, so anyone thinking to destroy the hive may suddenly find an human-insect monstrosity leaping out at them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T23:21:44-07:00","id":975391,"title":"","content":"I did have my Kushtaka earlier, who could be considered somewhere between an Otter Host and a true shifter. They don't devour each other, but they do hate the Gauntlet-and they reproduce by divide-and-merge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T23:55:24-07:00","id":975397,"title":"","content":"as for plant-based Hosts- what about a Cuscuta Host? The image of animated human corpses covered with twitching orange tentacle like things all connected to the same &quot;root&quot; is quit terrifying, and the plant does have a number of appropriate folk names.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T07:24:03-07:00","id":975502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/mai