ents":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T07:31:50-07:00","id":975505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=975274#post975274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Extravagant beehives, dripping with honey, but anything that tastes some slowly has bees manifest from inside their organs, effectively turning the victim into a sort of Bee Host as a step towards making them into a new hive. The victim actually forms the center of the hive, with the traditional hive structure built around them, so anyone thinking to destroy the hive may suddenly find an human-insect monstrosity leaping out at them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually pretty interesting, though human sized beehives seem pretty conspicuous xD How does the hives keep themselves from being discovered before the bee-hybrid is done developing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T07:38:13-07:00","id":975507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=975504#post975504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What are those? I'm not familiar with the plant</div> </div> </div> </div>check in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuscuta\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> in sort, it is a form of a parasitic plant which looks like a bunch of orange steams without leaves or roots. Their lack of chlorophyll means they can't make food for themselves, turning them into parasites. While they may look innocent at first, but if you leave them alone they could quickly cover whole field- so if you want to get rid of them, you have to burn the whole thing including the host. It also has some neat nicknames, like strangleweed, wizard's net, devil's hair or hellbine. Just replace the plant hosts with human ones and it is pure nightmare fuel.<br /> <br /> Also, it seems to really hate wheat (one of my university professors showed us a movie in which it &quot;grows away&quot; from the wheat as far as possible, preferring to starve to death because of some chemical the wheat spreads to the air), and it is also used to give some &quot;flavor&quot; to a beer. Two plot hooks ready to use, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T13:17:47-07:00","id":976693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=975507#post975507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">check in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuscuta\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> in sort, it is a form of a parasitic plant which looks like a bunch of orange steams without leaves or roots. Their lack of chlorophyll means they can't make food for themselves, turning them into parasites. While they may look innocent at first, but if you leave them alone they could quickly cover whole field- so if you want to get rid of them, you have to burn the whole thing including the host. It also has some neat nicknames, like strangleweed, wizard's net, devil's hair or hellbine. Just replace the plant hosts with human ones and it is pure nightmare fuel.<br /> <br /> Also, it seems to really hate wheat (one of my university professors showed us a movie in which it &quot;grows away&quot; from the wheat as far as possible, preferring to starve to death because of some chemical the wheat spreads to the air), and it is also used to give some &quot;flavor&quot; to a beer. Two plot hooks ready to use, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>that's pretty cool, though what is their motivation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T13:42:57-07:00","id":976719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/963801-possible-host-concepts?p=976693#post976693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> that's pretty cool, though what is their motivation?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that possibles urges would be to collect, spread, hide or drain. Each direction could be developed quit nicely, or maybe something more &quot;magical&quot; considering the connotations","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.th